    "body": "# What does this PR do?\n\nThe PPO trainer only checked the TRL version inside `CustomPPOTrainer.__init__`, after the model, dataset and reward model were already loaded. The error message told you to set `DISABLE_VERSION_CHECK=1`, but the check called transformers' `require_version` directly, so that variable did nothing.\n\nI moved the check to `_check_extra_dependencies` with `check_version(\"trl>=0.8.6,<=0.9.6\", mandatory=True)` for `stage=ppo`, and dropped the old one from the trainer. Now a wrong TRL version fails at argument parsing and tells you the required range and the install command.\n\nThis only makes PPO fail earlier, it doesn't fix PPO. `pyproject.toml` pins `trl>=0.18.0,<=0.24.0`, so PPO fails on every default install. Before, it failed after loading the models, now it fails right away. Actually making PPO work would need a separate env with `trl==0.9.6` or a port to the new TRL API. I left the pin alone.\n\nRelated to #10757\n\n## Before submitting\n\n- [x] Did you read the [contributor guideline](https://github.com/hiyouga/LlamaFactory/blob/main/.github/CONTRIBUTING.md)?\n- [x] Did you write any new necessary tests?",
